webhook.site	Intel::DOMAIN	threatdefence-numasec	numasec low: Legitimate request-collection service used to receive command output. Suspicious from production servers only numasec's interact tool falls back to webhook.site for out-of-band callbacks (FrancescoStabile/numasec). (ARTEX operators)	https://cloud.google.com/blog/topics/threat-intelligence/artex-and-friends-enter-agentic-offensive-frameworks
numasec-appsec-probe/1.2	Intel::SOFTWARE	threatdefence-numasec	numasec high: User agent of every request numasec's appsec_probe tool sends (SQL injection, XSS, login, IDOR and CORS candidate probes), which its appsec-web-triage runbook runs (numasec operators)	https://github.com/FrancescoStabile/numasec/blob/1237a2f3515aebbd5260383c7088aa0ea806b600/packages/numasec/src/tool/appsec-probe.ts#L218
numasec-knowledge-broker/1.2	Intel::SOFTWARE	threatdefence-numasec	numasec high: User agent of numasec's vulnerability-intelligence broker on the operator's host, to services.nvd.nist.gov, www.cisa.gov, api.first.org, api.osv.dev and api.github.com/advisories. HTTPS: proxy logs with TLS inspection (numasec operators)	https://github.com/FrancescoStabile/numasec/blob/1237a2f3515aebbd5260383c7088aa0ea806b600/packages/numasec/src/core/knowledge/broker.ts#L39
numasec	Intel::SOFTWARE	threatdefence-numasec	numasec medium: Exact user agent of numasec's page fetch tool when a Cloudflare challenge (403, cf-mitigated: challenge) blocked its first try with a Chrome 143 string. Short word: match the whole value (numasec operators)	https://github.com/FrancescoStabile/numasec/blob/1237a2f3515aebbd5260383c7088aa0ea806b600/packages/numasec/src/tool/webfetch.ts#L99
numasec/	Intel::SOFTWARE	threatdefence-numasec	numasec medium: Start of the user agents numasec sends from the operator's host: numasec/<channel>/<version>/<client> to models.dev/api.json (for example numasec/latest/1.2.1/cli) and numasec/<version> to model APIs. Inherited from OpenCode with the name changed. HTTPS: proxy logs with TLS inspection (numasec operators)	https://github.com/FrancescoStabile/numasec/blob/1237a2f3515aebbd5260383c7088aa0ea806b600/packages/numasec/src/installation/installation.ts#L57
api.github.com/repos/FrancescoStabile/numasec/releases/latest	Intel::URL	threatdefence-numasec	numasec medium: numasec update check for installs it cannot attribute to npm, bun, pnpm, brew, scoop or choco, one second after the TUI starts (npm installs ask registry.npmjs.org/numasec/latest). HTTPS: proxy logs with TLS inspection (numasec operators)	https://github.com/FrancescoStabile/numasec/blob/1237a2f3515aebbd5260383c7088aa0ea806b600/packages/numasec/src/installation/installation.ts#L250
numasec.ai	Intel::DOMAIN	threatdefence-numasec	numasec low: OpenCode's opencode.ai renamed in the numasec code: HTTP-Referer on OpenRouter, Vercel and ZenMux model calls, the CORS allow list of its API server, and https://numasec.ai/install, which the upgrade pipes into bash for curl installs. Ownership not verified and not contacted for this review (numasec operators)	https://github.com/FrancescoStabile/numasec/blob/1237a2f3515aebbd5260383c7088aa0ea806b600/packages/numasec/src/installation/installation.ts#L145
models.dev	Intel::DOMAIN	threatdefence-numasec	numasec low: Model catalogue numasec (and OpenCode, from which it inherits the call) fetches as /api.json at start and every five minutes at most. Shared with every OpenCode-based tool: context only (numasec operators)	https://github.com/FrancescoStabile/numasec/blob/1237a2f3515aebbd5260383c7088aa0ea806b600/packages/numasec/src/provider/models.ts#L111
